cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository, cite the software entry below. Individual
  criteria, their pre-registrations and their failures are recorded in
  RESULTS.md and in docs/; cite those by stage and criterion identifier
  (for example B8-3, A5-6) rather than by section number, because section
  numbers move and identifiers do not.
title: >-
  monetary-topology: mechanism models for a topological framework of
  claims and resources
abstract: >-
  Small mechanism models for a framework in which a monetary claim and the
  resource it points at are distinct objects. Each model isolates one
  mechanism, exposes fewer than a dozen parameters, and reports a criterion
  that can fail. Seven carriers, each a separate regulatory environment, have
  produced measured non-zero readings on real transaction data, each against a
  floor that is measured rather than asserted. Failed and withdrawn criteria are kept in the record
  alongside the passing ones.
type: software
